A. Triangular numbers mod 2^k: CRS on [0,2^k), fibres, windows, negative indices
====================================================================================================
  T_0..T_(2^k-1) is a CRS mod 2^k for k = 0..24 (cumsum generation): True
  Z/2^(k+1) -> Z/2^k is onto, exactly 2-to-1, fibres {n, 2^(k+1)-1-n}, k = 0..13: True
  window [a, a+2^k) is a CRS mod 2^k  <=>  a = 0 mod 2^k   (k = 1..9, -2^(k+1) <= a <= 2^(k+1)): True
     e.g. T_1..T_8 mod 8 = [1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 5, 6, 7]  (not a CRS: the count must start at T_0 = 0)
  T_(-1-n) = T_n for -5000 <= n < 5000: True

